 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Desktop operating system: 160-odd Linux/BSD/hobby names from old k9 redistributed into lineage archetypes (Linux distribution) and the hobby kind; Windows, macOS and ChromeOS are archetypes with versions/editions from fetched Wikipedia pages. Dropped as server, appliance, router, NAS, media-centre, phone or single-purpose systems: OpenWrt, VyOS, openmediavault, FreedomBox, Volumio, CoreELEC, LibreELEC, OSMC, Lakka, Recalbox, Batocera.linux, DietPi, Armbian, ZimaOS, Tribblix, openEuler, openKylin, LineageOS, Murena, postmarketOS, Mobian, Ubuntu Touch, also minor/dead or unplaced distros (Adelie, BigLinux, BlankOn, Bluefin, BunsenLabs, CAINE, Drauger OS, Elive, Emmabuntus, Exherbo, Feren OS, Finnix, Freespire, Linspire, Lindows, FydeOS, GNOME OS, Kicksecure, Kodachi, KDE neon, LinuxConsole, Nitrux, Obarun, Oreon, Pentoo, Peppermint OS, PikaOS, SliTaz, SolydXK, SystemRescue, TUXEDO OS, Ultramarine, Vanilla OS, Voyager, Wattos, antiX, blendOS, Linux Lite, Bodhi Linux, Damn Small Linux, Chimera, ChimeraOS). Classic Mac OS and other dead tails belong on the Classic software shelf. Virtual machine software cut from 50 to 17: dropped server/enterprise hypervisors (ESX/ESXi, XenServer, XCP-ng, Xen, PowerVM, z/VM, Virtuozzo, OpenVZ, OpenNebula, Oracle VM, Sun xVM, Virtual Iron, Wind River, PikeOS, LynxSecure, VirtualLogix, XtratuM, OKL4, RTS, Integrity VM), research/mainframe emulators (SIMH, GXemul, Hercules, Simics, CHARON, JPC, PearPC) and dead products (Virtual Server, VMware Server/ESX, Parallels Workstation, QuickTransit, SVISTA, Cooperative Linux, User Mode Linux, DOSEMU, LXC). UTM added from a fetched page. App compatibility layer cut from 21 to 11: dropped single-game or fringe wrappers (Sober, Vinegar, TeknoParrot, GameHub, MiceWine, libndk, libhoudini, Win3mu, NTVDMx64, Boxedwine). Brand entries use owner-approved knowledge."
